{"agent":"impl-drv-facts","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`assess` returns `state=\"unknown\"` when a fact has a version range but the installed version is missing or unparseable, but `pick` only skips facts for which `a.drifted` is true (expired/out_of_range). An unknown fact whose `s` is readable (or `s == \"none\"`) is still appended to `live`, so `facts.best` can return it. For example, with `installed=None` and candidates `[{\"s\": \"document\", \"v\": \"doc\"}, {\"s\": \"observation\", \"v\": \"obs\", \"versions\": \">=1.0\"}]`, the second fact assesses as `unknown`, is still considered live, and by the intended observation-outranks-document ranking `facts.best` returns it; `pick` then returns `Pick(value=\"obs\", fact=..., reason=\"\")` instead of skipping the unknown fact and returning the document or a fallback with the reason “installed version unknown…”. With only the unknown observation, it returns the observation value rather than the fallback, so the required unknown-degrades/report behavior is not implemented.","digest":"efa9641df1c28c67","location":"ddflow/services/factdrift.py:pick","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/factdrift.py:pick"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12183,"diff_sha":"39b3d3ca9528e64f826cee8c8a2bed0ae0160776ddbbfa5d4bae20520396ffc1","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":432.9,"family":"alibaba","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"2ac9ede29cb17d54","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DRV-facts.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261030T101634Z-753e3210.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"dca994643bc7b7d27a653336063f0689eb8383a7","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/factdrift.py":"100644 d794d6119c9da968f6