{"agent":"impl-drv-facts","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"The test name promises that a fact with `s=\"none\"` is *not* demoted below itself, but the assertion requires `factdrift.effective(fact(s=\"none\", expires=\"2020-01-01\"), today=TODAY)[\"s\"] == \"unverified\"`. That is the opposite of the stated invariant: an already-`none` fact should remain `\"none\"` rather than be changed to `\"unverified\"`. As written, the suite fails once `effective` correctly implements the “not demoted below itself” rule, and it conflicts with the later known-absence behavior for `s=\"none\"` in `test_none_fact_is_a_known_absence`.","digest":"4465e9307f10682c","location":"tests/test_facts_drift.py test_none_status_is_not_demoted_below_itself","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_facts_drift.py test_none_status_is_not_demoted_below_itself"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12692,"diff_sha":"6c623672020adfa330a277bac922cdf01a9a17f1a98e71817ed49096da4a70a9","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1052.7,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"97d786d0a6bf4434","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DRV-facts.critic.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261030T105553Z-6751ab19.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"cc6ee4a8f9fb2741e28e521551799fd9063852ec","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/factdrift.py":"100644 2ff018f029ce73525150d166e397480b6c2874de","ddflow/services/facts.py":"100644 508c88f276750f077872a80a2c3596ec61da8346","tests/test_facts_drift.py":"100644 4a973d9d018302753907ad8c5cd352f6bcde1294"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["tests/test_facts_drift.py test_none_status_is_not_demoted_below_itself"],"tree_sha":"eca05bcc7697+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e10fb7c6d46d4d1a06e6fc4f9","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":114399,"schema":1,"subject":"DRV-facts","ts":"2026-10-30T11:13:26.093546Z"}
{"agent":"impl-drv-facts","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`assess` is unprotected around `clock.parse_date(str(exp))`. A fact such as `{\"expires\": \"not-a-date\"}` causes `parse_date` to raise `ValueError`, so `assess`, and therefore `doctor`, `effective`, and `pick`, crash instead of returning an `Assessment` or a fallback reason. This is inconsistent with the invalid-version-range path, which catches `ValueError` at line 87 and degrades to `unknown`.","digest":"53bdbad8e090d6e6","location":"ddflow/services/factdrift.py:77","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/factdrift.py:77"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`test_none_status_is_not_demoted_below_itself` creates `fact(s=\"none\", expires=\"2020-01-01\")`. Because `fact()` defaults `\"v\": \"x\"`, this is a contradictory record: status `\"none\"` is a known absence and must carry `v=None` (as `test_none_fact_is_a_known_absence` correctly does at line 85), but this test leaves `v=\"x\"`. The assertion `factdrift.effective(f, today=TODAY)[\"s\"] == \"unverified\"` is therefore validated only for an invalid record that says “no value” and “x” simultaneously. The real case (`s=\"none\", v=None`) is not being tested; a correct implementation should leave a known absence alone or at least not regrade it into an unverified claim, but this test would pass while such a bug exists.","digest":"e06c1dde326fd0bb","location":"tests/test_facts_drift.py:66","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_facts_drift.py:66"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12909,"diff_sha":"543207ad415ea423f5789607f07e576d255e63a5bee26fe5191a0d34d9deaa6a","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":665.0,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"63addaf426e9958a","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DRV-facts.critic.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261030T110341Z-58f7fa0a.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"0be3f43df046cc42840bbd1b77b3decba4dad299","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/factdrift.py":"100644 a135aca0af0b79ce5abf2482a4a02d768fabf2ba","ddflow/services/facts.py":"100644 e67ad7e46b1e152ab8ff4260942202a527c580f0","tests/test_facts_drift.py":"100644 4a973d9d018302753907ad8c5cd352f6bcde1294"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/factdrift.py:77","tests/test_facts_drift.py:66"],"tree_sha":"eca05bcc7697+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e89ea2ec92e4a88715accaee3","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":114400,"schema":1,"subject":"DRV-facts","ts":"2026-10-30T11:14:46.583729Z"}
